# Snake Island — the forgotten fortnight

## Introduction

Snake Island lies upon Elmir Lake, north of Skull Keep, accessible by boat across waters in which immense serpents are said to move. A bearded gnomish patron comes to the Delvers Dungeon Guild carrying buckets of snakes and enough gold to tempt three bronze-ranked adventurers. He offers a thousand gold pieces to each of the Darkest Delvers for an expedition there. They accept, depart the following day and do not return for two weeks. When they arrive at the guild they are alive, adorned in unfamiliar clothing and rewards, but cannot explain much of what happened.[^journey]

## Fragments of the crossing

Their last common clear memory is a vast serpent rising out of mist above their little boat. Later recollections return in flashes: they row a dinghy through Elmir Lake, a mighty snake overturns it, and they wash ashore. Krandal wakes in a luxurious silk-draped room and uses a staff that becomes a python to defeat a viper. A snake princess called **Hissia** opens the door and calls him her love. He recalls a village with withered crops whose inhabitants demand the return of their stolen idol. A priest hands him a human-skull cup full of green liquid; its purpose is not disclosed.[^crand]

Evelyn glimpses herself before a multitude of cheering snakefolk, seated high upon a step pyramid while a serpentine official places a golden necklace and ring upon her. They call her queen, and she recalls giving a speech whose words are lost. Another flash shows a snake-handed warrior demanding a paladin's death at her hands. Koh remembers replacing a golden serpent idol with clay, only to be attacked by a corpse animated by a snake inside its mouth. The party also rides giant snakes into the mountains; Krandal and Evelyn are comfortable, while Koh needs a specially made saddle. Other scattered images include a poisoned princess, a rocky hillside broken by Koh's tumble and a bonfire around which ordinary snakes wield little spears and utensils as though preparing to eat captives. **No uninterrupted account establishes how these scenes fit together or whether every implied danger was overcome.**[^memories]

## The cliff above a volcano

As the Delvers return to their ordinary guild work, another glimpse interrupts Koh's thoughts. A small bearded patron is falling into a volcano, calling for a curse to be repaired. Koh hangs from the rock with a psychic knife driven into its surface, and Krandal sends his serpent staff to reach him. Evelyn, dressed as a snake queen, stands nearby. Koh remembers something useful from the terrifying moment: he has learned to shape **two psychic daggers at once**, though neither he nor the others now knows the entire chain of events. **The patron's fate and the curse's meaning remain unknown**.[^volcano]

## The gifts brought home

Krandal brings a **Staff of the Python** and new molting snake-scale mail. Koh has two curved serpent daggers in place of his old daggers, a **+1 Dagger of Venom**, four vials of venom and arrows resembling fossilized snakes. Evelyn wears a **Necklace of Adaptation** and **Ring of Poison Resistance**, initially impossible to remove until Cassius frees them from a magical binding. Flower garlands, mysterious scraps of letters and a gigantic fang accompany the return. The guild inspects the new equipment and releases it the next day, and the party receives its **3,000 gold total** for completing the assignment. The large golden idol seen in memory is not definitely among their possessions.[^rewards]

## Current status

**The Delvers have returned alive** and been paid by the guild, but **the bulk of the two-week expedition is missing from their memories**. The causes of amnesia, the princess's actual fate, whether Evelyn truly rules the island, the significance of the venom fang and the final state of the snakefolk remain **unresolved**. The separate world locations and items seen in recovered memories should not be treated as a complete explored map. The guild scene occurs at the **beginning of Season Two**, following the S1E12 offer. The party is now investigating its lives back in Atomer, not still sailing for Snake Island.[^status]

[^volcano]: [Delvers S2E02](../../episodes/S2E02.md), ~00:28–00:32. **GM explicitly acknowledges Koh's dual psychic blade ability in the current campaign**; scene is an intermittent lost-fortnight recall, not an unbroken volcano expedition or proven death of gnomish patron.
